---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Equipment Sourcing | Equip Solutions Group"
  description="Independent equipment sourcing for used, surplus and hard-to-find machines. Truck bodies, hooklifts, concrete equipment and agricultural machinery, verified and delivered.">

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap page-hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Independent sourcing desk</p>
      <h1>Equipment Sourcing</h1>
      <p>Not everything you need comes off a manufacturer's price list. Tell me the machine and the budget and I will work the dealer, auction and supplier network until something real comes back.</p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Start a search</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/parts/#agriculture">Looking for a part?</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">What this is</p>
          <h2 style="font-size:var(--step-3);text-transform:uppercase;">A buyer's agent for iron</h2>
          <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1rem;">Years of representing manufacturers means knowing who actually has inventory, who is honest about hours, and who will take a trade. That network does not switch off when the request falls outside a line I carry.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:1rem;color:var(--graphite);">You get one point of contact instead of nine listing sites, and a straight read on condition and price rather than a description written to sell.</p>
          <ul class="checks" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
            <li><strong>Used and surplus units</strong> &mdash; hooklifts, mixers, trailers, attachments and support equipment.</li>
            <li><strong>Hard-to-find machines</strong> &mdash; discontinued models and specific configurations.</li>
            <li><strong>Fleet additions</strong> &mdash; matching what you already run so parts and training carry over.</li>
            <li><strong>Trade and disposal</strong> &mdash; finding a home for the unit you are replacing.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="ph ph--tall">Photo &mdash; equipment yard or units lined up<br>Recommended 900&times;1200</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Process</p>
        <h2>How a search runs</h2>
        <p>Sourcing is legwork, not luck. Here is the order it happens in and what you get at each stage.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <span class="step-n">01</span>
          <h3>Define the target</h3>
          <p>Machine, spec, acceptable hours or condition, delivery window and a real budget ceiling. Vague searches return vague results.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="step-n">02</span>
          <h3>Work the network</h3>
          <p>Dealers, auctions, upfitters, fleet turnovers and manufacturer contacts &mdash; including units that never get listed publicly.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="step-n">03</span>
          <h3>Verify before you look</h3>
          <p>Photos, hours, service history and a candid read on condition. Bad candidates get filtered out before they reach you.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="step-n">04</span>
          <h3>Land it</h3>
          <p>Price negotiated, freight quoted, inspection or transport coordinated, paperwork handled through delivery.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="plate-grid plate-grid--3">
        <div class="plate">
          <div class="plate-code">Category</div>
          <h3>Truck &amp; Body</h3>
          <p>Hooklift hoists, roll-off units, dump bodies, flatbeds, containers, subframes and trailers &mdash; new, used or coming off a fleet.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="plate">
          <div class="plate-code">Category</div>
          <h3>Concrete &amp; Aggregate</h3>
          <p>Volumetric plants, cement silos, dispensers, conveyors, pumps and the support equipment around a batching operation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="plate">
          <div class="plate-code">Category</div>
          <h3>Agriculture</h3>
          <p>Implements, attachments and used machinery, plus the parts side that keeps older equipment in the field instead of in a fencerow.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark on-dark">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Ground rules</p>
        <h2>What you can expect from me</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="checks">
        <li><strong>No search fee to start.</strong> Tell me what you need and I will tell you honestly whether I can find it.</li>
        <li><strong>Condition described straight.</strong> If it is rough, you hear it is rough. A bad buy costs me the next five calls.</li>
        <li><strong>Freight quoted with the unit.</strong> Delivered cost, not a number that grows after you say yes.</li>
        <li><strong>A real answer on timing.</strong> If the market is dry for what you want, I will say so rather than string it out.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Tell me what you are looking for</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    heading="Describe the machine. I will go find it."
    body="Model, spec, budget and when you need it on the ground. Photos help if you are matching something you already run.">
    <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Start a search</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="tel:+15157200800">Call +1 515 720 0800</a>
  </CtaBand>

</BaseLayout>
